 Features of java :

 
 Simple: Java has easy syntax and removes complex features like explicit pointers.

Object-Oriented: Java is based on classes and objects and supports the four OOP principles.

Platform Independent: Java follows WORA (Write Once, Run Anywhere) using bytecode and JVM.

Secure: Java provides bytecode verification, access control, and security APIs.

Robust: Java provides exception handling, garbage collection, and strong type checking.

Multithreaded: Java allows multiple tasks to execute concurrently using threads.

Portable: Java programs can run on different operating systems with minimal or no changes.

Architecture Neutral: Java bytecode is independent of any specific processor architecture.

High Performance: Java uses JIT compilation to improve execution speed.

Distributed: Java supports network-based applications using networking APIs.

Dynamic: Java can load and link classes at runtime.

Interpreted and Compiled: Java compiler converts source code into bytecode, which JVM interprets or JIT-compiles.
